James sought guidance on integrating feedback related to reallocating spending away from environmentally harmful subsidies within a chapter focused on climate adaptation investments. The discussion highlighted the importance of not only investing in new adaptive measures but also reassessing existing financial priorities that encourage unsustainable practices. Arachne suggested placing this content under the section “Strategic trade-offs in adaptation,” emphasizing that redirecting funds from harmful subsidies can enhance resilience and foster sustainable economic growth. This proposed addition reinforced the chapter's themes of proactive investment and holistic economic policy refinement.
